-- title:
--   Symmetric 2-cocycles span: at most h-n classes modulo coboundaries
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, let $n$ be a natural number and let $F_0$ be an $n$-dimensional formal group law over $k$: an $n$-tuple of power series in two blocks of $n$ variables, each with zero constant term, whose linear terms in the two blocks are $X_i$ and $Y_i$ respectively, satisfying the associativity identity $F_0(F_0(X,Y),Z) = F_0(X,F_0(Y,Z))$; assume $F_0$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Let $h$ be a natural number and assume that the quotient of $k[\![X_1,\dots,X_n]\!]$ by the ideal generated by the $n$ components of the $p$-fold iterate $[p]_{F_0}$, defined by iterating $m \mapsto F_0(\cdot,X)$ from $0$ exactly $p$ times, has $k$-dimension $p^h$. Call a power series $\Gamma$ in the two blocks of variables a symmetric two-cocycle for $F_0$ when $\Gamma(0,0)=0$, $\Gamma(Y,X)=\Gamma(X,Y)$ and $\Gamma(F_0(X,Y),Z)+\Gamma(X,Y)=\Gamma(X,F_0(Y,Z))+\Gamma(Y,Z)$, and write $\partial g(X,Y)=g(F_0(X,Y))-g(X)-g(Y)$. Then there exist an $r$ with $r \le h - n$ (truncated subtraction in $\mathbb{N}$) and symmetric two-cocycles $\Gamma_1,\dots,\Gamma_r$ for $F_0$ such that every symmetric two-cocycle $\Gamma'$ for $F_0$ can be written as $\Gamma' = \sum_j c_j \Gamma_j + \partial g$ with $c_j \in k$ and $g$ a power series in one block of variables with zero constant term. No linear independence of the $\Gamma_j$ is asserted.
--
--   The symmetric two-cocycles modulo coboundaries classify commutative extensions of $F_0$ by the additive formal group, so the statement is the inequality $\dim_k \mathrm{Ext}^1(F_0,\mathbb{G}_a) \le h-n$ for a commutative formal group law of dimension $n$ and height $h$, in the form of an explicit spanning family. It feeds the deformation-theoretic results over the dual numbers for formal groups and for special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Cherednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_isSymmTwoCocycle_span_of_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_eq_pow.lean

